# {{ plugin_name }}

Independent RVST {{ kind }} plugin by {{ vendor }}. This repository owns the
processor, shared UI, native exports, standalone app, browser runner and xtask.

```sh
cargo build --locked
cargo test --workspace --locked
cargo fmt --all --check
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings
cargo xtask bundle --release
```

For local development with live browser logs:

```sh
cargo run -p plugin-standalone --features devtools
# In another terminal, if cargo-rvst is installed:
cargo rvst inspect --open
```

The standalone runs real native audio. The browser preview uses the same Rust
editor against a simulated host; browser DSP is intentionally disabled.

```sh
rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown
cargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version 0.2.130 --locked
cargo xtask web --serve --open
```

Record/replay a deterministic offline fixture, including MIDI and block boundaries:

```sh
cargo xtask record capture.json --blocks 64
cargo xtask replay capture.json --step
```

`cargo xtask install` explicitly installs development bundles into user plugin
folders. `cargo xtask bundle --release` creates bundles without installing them.
Add `--target`, `--profile` or `--features` when needed. Native debugging uses the
included `.vscode/launch.json` CodeLLDB configurations, or `lldb --
target/debug/plugin-standalone` (`gdb --args` on Linux). Chrome inspects the live
logs and browser UI; source stepping native DSP requires the native debugger.

SDK source: `{{ sdk_source }}`. Registry dependencies require a published RVST
release. Before publication use an explicit SDK override or a vendored snapshot.
The provenance files record template inputs, identities and source. Keep the
plugin ID and VST3 class identity unchanged after release, including renames.

No global RVST tool is required for the Cargo commands above. Qualify actual
bundles with VST3/CLAP validators and real DAWs before distributing a release.
Tests and compilation alone do not establish host compatibility.
